title: 'no relay-aware receive path: monitor ignores the relay inbox; subscribe rejects wss; connect broken — only hand-rolled poll works'
---
An agent cannot receive cross-host messages through one supported command. c2c monitor watches only the local broker, never the relay inbox. relay subscribe refuses wss/HTTPS. relay connect is broken (see relay-connect bug). The only working path is a hand-rolled relay dm poll loop. Ship a first-class relay-aware monitor (poll-based is fine for now) so relay DMs surface like local ones; long term unify local+relay in one monitor. Related: B043 (local monitor e2e), B070 (archive-only). Source: friction-points-cn.md.